-- allium: 3
-- pulls.allium — pull requests: proposing a head branch for a base branch, checking it, reviewing it and merging it.
--
-- Scope: the lifecycle of a pull request from opening (same repository, from a
--   fork, or by an AGit `refs/for/` push) through mergeability checking, head and
--   base updates, review and review requests, code conversations and suggested
--   changes, merge preconditions (repository merge settings and branch
--   protection), merging in every style, scheduled auto-merge, closing,
--   reopening, retargeting and head-branch cleanup.
-- Includes: PullRequest, Review, ReviewRequest, CodeConversation, ReviewComment,
--   AutoMerge, FileViewState, CodeOwnerRule; the MergeStyle and UpdateStyle
--   enums; mergeability checking; merge-message composition; CODEOWNERS
--   auto-requests; maintainer edits on fork pull requests.
-- Excludes:
--   - The conversation half of a pull request (title, description, labels,
--     milestone, assignees, deadline, lock, pin, reactions, plain timeline
--     comments, subscriptions, time tracking, dependencies): owned by issues.
--     Pinning a pull request is issues/IssuePin. issues closes the
--     conversation on PullRequestMerged and applies closing keywords; this
--     module sets `issue.status` for PR-specific close/reopen (with guards) and
--     creates the pulls-owned timeline Comment kinds.
--   - The pull-request unit settings of a repository (allowed merge styles,
--     autodetect manual merge, allow rebase update, defaults): owned by
--     repositories (RepoUnit.pull_request_settings); read here through
--     merge_style_allowed() and autodetects_manual_merge().
--   - Branch protection rule management (create/edit/delete rules, push
--     allowlists, protected-file rejection on push): owned by code. This module
--     only reads the merge-related fields of code/ProtectedBranch.
--   - Commit statuses and their reporting API: owned by code (CommitStatus);
--     read here through required_status_checks_pass().
--   - Git transport, pre/post-receive hooks and AGit parsing of push options as
--     transport: owned by code; this module owns what an AGit push *does* to a
--     pull request (open or update) and the pull-ref push rules.
--   - Signing keys and the merge signing policy (`[repository.signing] MERGES`):
--     owned by keys; read here through merge_signing_satisfied().
--   - Actions trust decisions for fork pull requests ("approve workflows",
--     trust poster): owned by actions.
--   - Git notes on pull-request commits (`/pulls/{index}/commits/{sha}/notes`):
--     a commit concern owned by code.
--   - Compare view for arbitrary refs (`/compare/a...b` without opening a PR)
--     and diff rendering options (split/unified, whitespace, file tree, image
--     and CSV diff, blob excerpts): presentation, owned by code/discovery. Only
--     the behaviour-relevant diff limits are kept as config here.
--   - LFS object propagation on merge/update: storage plumbing.
--   - The merge-check and auto-merge queues, their restart re-queueing
--     (`InitializePullRequests`) and the per-PR working lock: infrastructure;
--     the spec models the check as an asynchronous step (check_requested_at).
--   - Migrated reviews (`original_author`) and Gitea "PullRequestType": data
--     import / legacy, not behaviour.
--   - Notifications, mail, webhooks, activity feed entries: reacted to by those
--     modules from the triggers below.
--
-- Emits:
--   PullRequestOpened(pull_request)
--   PullRequestSynchronized(pull_request, doer)        -- head moved (webhook "synchronized", actions)
--   PullRequestHeadUpdated(pull_request, pusher, old_commit_sha, new_commit_sha, is_force_push)
--                                                      -- the "pushed commits" timeline entry (notifications)
--   PullRequestTargetBranchChanged(pull_request, doer, old_base_branch)
--   PullRequestClosed(pull_request, doer)              -- doer is null when a repository deletion closed it
--   PullRequestReopened(pull_request, doer)
--   PullRequestReadyForReview(pull_request, doer)      -- WIP prefix removed from the title
--   PullRequestBranchUpdated(pull_request, doer, style) -- head updated from base ("update branch")
--   PullRequestMerged(pull_request, merger)            -- also for manual merges; style in pull_request.merge_style
--                                                      -- issues closes the conversation and applies closing keywords
--   PullRequestAutoMerged(pull_request, merger)        -- emitted together with PullRequestMerged
--   AutoMergeScheduled(pull_request, doer) / AutoMergeCancelled(pull_request, doer)
--   ReviewSubmitted(review)                            -- review.pull_request; approvals re-evaluate auto-merge
--   PullRequestCodeCommented(pull_request, comment)
--   ReviewRequested(pull_request, requester, reviewer)
--   ReviewRequestRemoved(pull_request, doer, reviewer)
--   TeamReviewRequested(pull_request, requester, team) -- notified to each member except the poster
--   TeamReviewRequestRemoved(pull_request, doer, team)
--   ReviewDismissed(review, dismisser, message)
--   PullRequestHeadBranchDeleted(pull_request, doer)
--   HeadBranchDeletionRequested(user, branch)          -- code deletes the head branch as UserDeletesBranch does
--   SuggestionsApplied(pull_request, doer, conversations)
--   IssueClosedByPullRequest(issue, pull_request, doer)   -- per issue the merged PR closes by keyword
--   IssueReopenedByPullRequest(issue, pull_request, doer) -- per issue the merged PR reopens by keyword
--
-- Reacts to:
--   code/CommitsPushed(repository, branch_name, pusher, old_sha, new_sha, is_force)
--                                       -- head pushes update PRs; base pushes re-check PRs
--   code/AgitPullRequestRequested(repository, pusher, base_branch, head_branch, head_sha, title, description)
--   code/AgitPullRequestHeadPushed(pull, pusher, old_sha, new_sha)
--   code/MergePushCompleted(pull, pusher, merge_commit_sha)
--   code/BranchDeleted(branch, by)      -- open PRs from/into the branch are closed
--   code/BranchRenamed(repository, from_name, to_name, by)  -- unmerged PRs follow the rename
--   code/BranchProtectionChanged(rule)  -- PRs into matching branches are re-checked
--   code/CommitStatusCreated(status)    -- (through AutoMerge.is_ready) auto-merge re-evaluates
--   issues/IssueTitleChanged(issue, doer, old_title)  -- WIP prefix removed => ready for review
--   repositories/RepositoryDeleted(repository, doer)  -- PRs from its branches into other repos close
--   accounts/UserRenamed(user, old_name, new_name)    -- AGit head branch names follow the poster

use "./accounts.allium" as accounts
use "./organizations.allium" as organizations
use "./repositories.allium" as repositories
use "./access.allium" as access
use "./code.allium" as code
use "./issues.allium" as issues

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Black-box predicates and functions used below
------------------------------------------------------------
-- Permissions (thin local names for access semantics, so journeys can state them):
--   can_read_pulls(user, repository)  = access/can_read(user, repository, pull_requests)
--   can_write_pulls(user, repository) = access/can_write(user, repository, pull_requests)
--   can_read_code(user, repository)   = access/can_read(user, repository, code)
--   can_write_code(user, repository)  = access/can_write(user, repository, code)
--   is_repo_admin(user, repository)   = access/is_repo_admin(user, repository)
--   is_repository_owner(user, repository), is_collaborator(user, repository),
--   in_team_reading_pulls(user, repository): owner / repositories/Collaboration /
--       member of an organization team with read access to the pull-request unit
--   is_blocked_by_owner(repository, user) = the owner (user or org) blocks user (accounts/UserBlock)
--   is_team_member(user, team), team_has_repository(team, repository),
--   is_organization(user), is_organization_owned(repository): organizations
-- Repository pull-request settings (repositories/RepoUnit.pull_request_settings):
--   merge_style_allowed(repository, style) = the matching allow_* flag
--       (allow_merge, allow_rebase, allow_rebase_merge, allow_squash,
--       allow_fast_forward_only, allow_manual_merge)
--   autodetects_manual_merge(repository) = autodetect_manual_merge
-- Branch protection (code):
--   protection_for(repository, branch) -> code/ProtectedBranch?   first matching rule
--   rule_matches_branch(rule, branch_name)
--   branch_is_protected(repository, branch_name) = protection_for(...) != null
--   required_status_checks_pass(pr): every status_check_contexts glob matches at
--       least one commit status of the head commit and the worst matching state
--       is success; with no contexts configured, the combined status is success
--   team_is_official_reviewer(team, pr): with a rule, the team is on the
--       approvals allowlist (or, allowlist disabled, has code write); without a
--       rule, never
-- Git (code):
--   branch_exists(repository, name) = a live code/Branch exists
--   head_commit_of(repository, branch), commit_in_branch(repository, branch, sha),
--   full_commit_sha(repository, sha), commit_authored_at(repository, sha),
--   is_force_push(repository, old_sha, new_sha), is_related_fork(head_repo, base_repo),
--   commits_ahead_of / commits_behind_of(head_repo, head_branch, base_repo, base_branch),
--   commits_between(...), commits_between_shas(...)
--   merge_check_outcome(pr) -> MergeCheckOutcome, merge_base_of(pr),
--   conflicting_files(pr), protected_files_changed(pr), merge_commit_containing(pr),
--   manual_merge_author(pr), merge_result_commit(pr, style, message),
--   updated_head(pr, style), suggestion_commit(pr, threads, summary, message)
--   diff_differs(pr, old_sha, new_sha): the head-vs-base diff changed
--   anchored_lines_changed(conversation, sha), blamed_commit(...), diff_hunk_around(...)
--   head_equals_branch(pr, branch): the head commit equals that branch's tip
-- Pull requests (this module):
--   open_pull_request_exists(head_repo, head_branch, base_repo, base_branch): an open unmerged PR
--       with that head and base exists (of the same flow as the one being opened/reopened)
--   open_pull_requests_into(repository, branch) -> Set<PullRequest>
--   has_other_open_pull_request_from(pr): another open PR uses the same head branch
--   has_wip_prefix(title): title starts, case-insensitively, with one of
--       config.work_in_progress_prefixes
--   latest_blocking_review_of(pr, reviewer) -> Review?  (newest approve/request_changes)
--   has_submitted_review(pr, reviewer)
--   may_update_by_merge(user, pr), may_update_by_rebase(user, pr): see UserUpdatesPullRequestBranch
--   suggestion_applicable(conversation, head_sha), suggestions_overlap(conversations)
--   count_suggestions(body): number of ```suggestion blocks
--   code_owner_users(rules, pr), code_owner_teams(rules, pr)
--   compose_merge_message(pr, style, title, message), default_merge_message(pr, style)
--   issues_closed_by(pr) / issues_reopened_by(pr) -> Set<issues/Issue>: the issues whose
--       latest keyword reference from this PR (issues/Comment with ref_issue = pr.issue
--       and ref_action closes / reopens) is a close / reopen; one entry per issue
--   agit_head_branch / rename_agit_head_branch: "<lowercase user name>/<topic>"
-- Elsewhere:
--   has_open_blocking_dependencies(issue): issues dependencies enabled and an open blocker exists
--   merge_signing_satisfied(pr, user, style): keys (see Requests)
--   within_quota(repository): quota, size:git:all of the repository owner
--   next_issue_index(repository): issues
--   trimmed_length(text), truncate(text, n)

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- How a pull request's commits land on the base branch.
-- from: models/repo/git.go:13
enum MergeStyle {
    merge                -- merge commit (--no-ff)
    | rebase             -- rebase head onto base, fast-forward base
    | rebase_merge       -- rebase head onto base, then a merge commit
    | squash             -- one squashed commit authored by the PR poster
    | fast_forward_only  -- fast-forward base to head or fail
    | manually_merged    -- not a git operation: the PR is marked as already merged
}

-- How "update branch" brings base changes into the head branch.
-- from: models/repo/git.go:28
enum UpdateStyle { merge | rebase }

-- Where the head of a pull request lives.
-- `branch`: a branch of the base repository or of a related fork.
-- `agit`: no head branch; the head is the pull ref written by an AGit push.
-- from: models/issues/pull.go:138
enum PullRequestFlow { branch | agit }

-- Result of one mergeability check (black box over git; see CheckMergeability).
-- from: services/pull/patch.go:162
enum MergeCheckOutcome {
    clean            -- merges cleanly and changes something
    | conflicting    -- three-way merge has conflicts
    | no_changes     -- merges cleanly but the merged tree equals the base tree
    | already_in_base  -- the head commit is already contained in the base branch
    | failed         -- the check itself could not run
}

-- The verdict a reviewer submits.
-- from: models/issues/review.go:74
enum ReviewVerdict { approve | comment | request_changes }

-- Which side of the diff a code conversation is anchored to.
-- from: routers/web/repo/pull_review.go:89
enum DiffSide { previous | proposed }

-- Per-user, per-file review progress on the "files changed" view.
-- from: models/pull/review_state.go:16
enum FileViewedState { unviewed | has_changed | viewed }


------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities and Variants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A proposal to bring head_branch (of head_repository) into base_branch (of
-- base_repository). Its conversation (title, description, open/closed,
-- timeline) is an issues/Issue with is_pull = true.
-- from: models/issues/pull.go:146
entity PullRequest {
    issue: issues/Issue
    flow: PullRequestFlow
    head_repository: repositories/Repository
    head_branch: String               -- for agit: "<poster lowercase name>/<topic>"
    base_repository: repositories/Repository
    base_branch: String
    head_commit_sha: String           -- the commit the pull ref (refs/pull/<index>/head) points at
    merge_base_sha: String?
    created_at: Timestamp

    -- Mergeability. `checking` is entered whenever head or base moves and left
    -- by CheckMergeability. merged / manually_merged are terminal.
    status: checking | mergeable | conflict | empty | ancestor | error | merged | manually_merged
    check_requested_at: Timestamp?    -- set while a check is queued
    last_check_outcome: MergeCheckOutcome?
    conflicted_files: Set<String>
    changed_protected_files: Set<String>  -- at most config.max_reported_protected_files
    commits_ahead: Integer
    commits_behind: Integer

    allow_maintainer_edit: Boolean    -- "allow edits from maintainers" (fork PRs)

    merged_commit_sha: String when status = merged | manually_merged
    merge_style: MergeStyle when status = merged | manually_merged
    merger: accounts/User when status = merged | manually_merged
    merged_at: Timestamp when status = merged | manually_merged
    -- true only when a scheduled auto-merge performed the merge; consumers that
    -- react to both PullRequestMerged and PullRequestAutoMerged use it to avoid
    -- announcing one merge twice
    merged_automatically: Boolean when status = merged | manually_merged

    transitions status {
        checking -> mergeable
        checking -> conflict
        checking -> empty
        checking -> ancestor
        checking -> error
        checking -> manually_merged
        mergeable -> checking
        conflict -> checking
        empty -> checking
        ancestor -> checking
        error -> checking
        mergeable -> merged
        empty -> merged
        mergeable -> manually_merged
        conflict -> manually_merged
        empty -> manually_merged
        ancestor -> manually_merged
        error -> manually_merged
        terminal: merged, manually_merged
    }

    -- Relationships
    reviews: Review with pull_request = this
    review_requests: ReviewRequest with pull_request = this
    conversations: CodeConversation with pull_request = this
    auto_merge: AutoMerge with pull_request = this
    file_view_states: FileViewState with pull_request = this

    -- Projections
    submitted_reviews: reviews where status = submitted
    official_approvals: reviews where kind = approve and is_official = true and is_dismissed = false
    fresh_official_approvals: official_approvals where is_stale = false
    official_rejections: reviews where kind = request_changes and is_official = true and is_dismissed = false
    official_review_requests: review_requests where is_official = true
    open_conversations: conversations where resolved_by = null
    current_conversations: conversations where is_outdated = false

    -- Derived
    is_open: issue.status = open
    is_merged: status = merged or status = manually_merged
    is_checking: status = checking
    is_from_fork: head_repository != base_repository
    is_work_in_progress: has_wip_prefix(issue.title)
    head_branch_present: flow = agit or branch_exists(head_repository, head_branch)
    base_branch_present: branch_exists(base_repository, base_branch)
    is_ready_for_merge_state: status = mergeable or status = empty

    -- The first branch-protection rule of the base repository matching the base
    -- branch (exact names win over globs; earliest-created glob otherwise).
    protection: protection_for(base_repository, base_branch)
    -- The pull-request unit settings of the base repository allow this style.
    allows_style(style): merge_style_allowed(base_repository, style)
    counts_only_fresh_approvals: protection != null and protection.ignore_stale_approvals
    approval_count: if counts_only_fresh_approvals: fresh_official_approvals.count else: official_approvals.count
    required_checks_pass: protection = null or not protection.status_check_enabled or required_status_checks_pass(this)
    has_enough_approvals: protection = null or approval_count >= protection.required_approvals
    blocked_by_rejection: protection != null and protection.block_on_rejected_reviews and official_rejections.count > 0
    blocked_by_official_requests: protection != null and protection.block_on_official_review_requests and official_review_requests.count > 0
    blocked_by_outdated_branch: protection != null and protection.block_on_outdated_branch and commits_behind > 0
    blocked_by_protected_files: protection != null and protection.protected_file_patterns.count > 0 and changed_protected_files.count > 0
    protection_satisfied: required_checks_pass and has_enough_approvals
        and not blocked_by_rejection and not blocked_by_official_requests
        and not blocked_by_outdated_branch and not blocked_by_protected_files

    -- Who may merge: without protection, code writers of the base repository;
    -- with protection, the rule's merge allowlist (or code writers when the
    -- allowlist is disabled).
    may_merge(u): if protection = null: can_write_code(u, base_repository) else: protection.allows_merge_by(u)
    -- "Merge anyway": instance admins always; repository admins unless the rule
    -- applies to admins.
    may_bypass_protection(u): u.is_admin or (protection != null and not protection.apply_to_admins and is_repo_admin(u, base_repository))
    -- An official review counts towards required approvals.
    is_official_reviewer(u): if protection = null: can_write_code(u, base_repository) else: protection.counts_approval_of(u)
    -- Poster, repository owner, collaborators, and members of org teams with
    -- read access to pull requests may change review requests.
    may_change_review_requests(u): u = issue.poster or is_repository_owner(u, base_repository)
        or is_collaborator(u, base_repository) or in_team_reading_pulls(u, base_repository)
    -- Poster or pull-request writers.
    may_manage(u): u = issue.poster or can_write_pulls(u, base_repository)
    -- Poster, pull-request writers and official reviewers resolve conversations.
    may_resolve_conversations(u): u = issue.poster or can_write_pulls(u, base_repository) or is_official_reviewer(u)
    -- Push to the head branch: code writers of the head repository, or base
    -- code writers when the poster allowed maintainer edits and the poster can
    -- still write the head repository.
    may_push_to_head(u): can_write_code(u, head_repository)
        or (allow_maintainer_edit and can_write_code(issue.poster, head_repository) and can_write_code(u, base_repository))
    head_is_editable_by(u): flow = branch and is_open and not is_merged
        and not head_repository.is_mirror and may_push_to_head(u)

    invariant AgitHeadsLiveInTheBaseRepository {
        flow = agit implies head_repository = base_repository
    }
}

-- A reviewer's feedback on a pull request. A review starts `pending` (a draft
-- only its author sees, collecting code comments) and becomes submitted with a
-- verdict. Review *requests* are ReviewRequest, not Review.
-- from: models/issues/review.go:102
entity Review {
    pull_request: PullRequest
    reviewer: accounts/User
    status: pending | submitted
    kind: ReviewVerdict when status = submitted
    body: String
    commit_sha: String               -- head commit the review was made against
    is_official: Boolean             -- counts towards required approvals (only the latest approve/request_changes per reviewer)
    is_stale: Boolean                -- the PR diff changed since commit_sha
    is_dismissed: Boolean
    created_at: Timestamp
    submitted_at: Timestamp when status = submitted

    transitions status {
        pending -> submitted
        terminal: submitted
    }

    conversations: CodeConversation with review = this
    comments: ReviewComment with review = this

    is_pending: status = pending
    is_blocking_verdict: status = submitted and (kind = approve or kind = request_changes)
}

-- A request for a user or a team to review. Removed when the requested user
-- submits a review (or, for teams, when a member approves / requests changes).
-- from: models/issues/review.go:547
entity ReviewRequest {
    pull_request: PullRequest
    reviewer: accounts/User?             -- exactly one of reviewer / team is set
    team: organizations/Team?
    requested_by: accounts/User
    is_official: Boolean                 -- the requested party would count towards approvals
    created_at: Timestamp
}

-- A thread of review comments anchored to a line range of a file in the diff.
-- Conversations belong to one review; replies join the thread.
-- from: models/issues/comment_code.go:17
entity CodeConversation {
    pull_request: PullRequest
    review: Review
    path: String
    line: Integer                    -- first line of the range on `side`
    side: DiffSide
    extra_lines: Integer             -- range spans line .. line + extra_lines
    commit_sha: String               -- commit whose blame anchors the range
    diff_hunk: String                -- context lines captured at creation
    is_outdated: Boolean             -- the anchored lines changed in a later head
    resolved_by: accounts/User?

    comments: ReviewComment with conversation = this
    is_resolved: resolved_by != null
}

-- One comment in a code conversation (pulls' "code comment"). May carry at most
-- one ```suggestion block replacing the anchored lines.
-- from: services/pull/review.go:131
entity ReviewComment {
    conversation: CodeConversation
    review: Review
    poster: accounts/User
    body: String
    created_at: Timestamp

    suggestion_count: count_suggestions(body)
    has_suggestion: suggestion_count > 0
}

-- A pull request scheduled to merge as soon as it becomes mergeable and its
-- required status checks succeed. At most one per pull request.
-- from: models/pull/automerge.go:16
entity AutoMerge {
    pull_request: PullRequest
    scheduled_by: accounts/User
    style: MergeStyle
    message: String
    delete_branch_after_merge: Boolean
    created_at: Timestamp

    is_ready: pull_request.status = mergeable and pull_request.is_open
        and pull_request.required_checks_pass and pull_request.head_branch_present
}

-- A user's viewed/unviewed mark for one changed file at one head commit. Files
-- marked viewed at an older head whose content changed since then show as
-- has_changed.
-- from: models/pull/review_state.go:26
entity FileViewState {
    pull_request: PullRequest
    user: accounts/User
    commit_sha: String
    path: String
    state: FileViewedState
    updated_at: Timestamp
}

-- One line of a CODEOWNERS file on the base repository's default branch
-- (looked up at CODEOWNERS, docs/CODEOWNERS, .gitea/CODEOWNERS,
-- .forgejo/CODEOWNERS, first found wins). `pattern` is an anchored regular
-- expression over changed paths; `!` negates. Owners are @user or @org/team.
-- from: models/issues/pull.go:788
entity CodeOwnerRule {
    repository: repositories/Repository
    pattern: String
    is_negated: Boolean
    users: Set<accounts/User>
    teams: Set<organizations/Team>
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    -- [repository.pull-request] WORK_IN_PROGRESS_PREFIXES (case-insensitive title prefixes)
    work_in_progress_prefixes: List<String> = ["WIP:", "[WIP]"]
    -- [repository.pull-request] CLOSE_KEYWORDS / REOPEN_KEYWORDS (used by issues' reference parser and the merge message)
    close_keywords: List<String> = ["close", "closes", "closed", "fix", "fixes", "fixed", "resolve", "resolves", "resolved"]
    reopen_keywords: List<String> = ["reopen", "reopens", "reopened"]
    -- [repository.pull-request] DEFAULT_MERGE_STYLE
    default_merge_style: MergeStyle = merge
    -- [repository.pull-request] DEFAULT_UPDATE_STYLE
    default_update_style: UpdateStyle = merge
    -- [repository.pull-request] DEFAULT_MERGE_MESSAGE_COMMITS_LIMIT (squash message commit scan; -1 = unlimited)
    default_merge_message_commits_limit: Integer = 50
    -- [repository.pull-request] DEFAULT_MERGE_MESSAGE_SIZE (bytes of commit messages in a squash message; also the merge-template read limit)
    default_merge_message_size: Integer = 5120
    -- [repository.pull-request] DEFAULT_MERGE_MESSAGE_ALL_AUTHORS (Co-authored-by for authors beyond the commit limit)
    default_merge_message_all_authors: Boolean = false
    -- [repository.pull-request] DEFAULT_MERGE_MESSAGE_MAX_APPROVERS (Reviewed-by lines; 0 = none, -1 = all)
    default_merge_message_max_approvers: Integer = 10
    -- [repository.pull-request] DEFAULT_MERGE_MESSAGE_OFFICIAL_APPROVERS_ONLY
    default_merge_message_official_approvers_only: Boolean = true
    -- [repository.pull-request] POPULATE_SQUASH_COMMENT_WITH_COMMIT_MESSAGES
    populate_squash_comment_with_commit_messages: Boolean = false
    -- [repository.pull-request] RETARGET_CHILDREN_ON_MERGE
    retarget_children_on_merge: Boolean = true
    -- [git] PULL_REQUEST_PUSH_MESSAGE: tell pushers the PR / create-PR link
    pull_request_push_message: Boolean = true
    -- [ui] CODE_COMMENT_LINES: diff context captured around a code comment
    code_comment_context_lines: Integer = 4
    -- [ui] MAX_CODE_COMMENT_LINES: longest line range one code comment may span (0 = no limit)
    max_code_comment_lines: Integer = 50
    -- [ui] MAX_DISPLAY_FILE_SIZE: CODEOWNERS read limit and largest file a suggestion may edit
    max_display_file_size: Integer = 8388608
    -- [git] MAX_GIT_DIFF_LINES / MAX_GIT_DIFF_LINE_CHARACTERS: per-file diff truncation in views
    max_diff_lines: Integer = 1000
    max_diff_line_characters: Integer = 5000
    -- [ui] DIFF_PAGING_NUM? (files per page on "files changed")
    diff_files_per_page: Integer = 20
    -- fixed limits
    max_title_length: Integer = 255
    max_suggestions_per_apply: Integer = 100
    max_reported_protected_files: Integer = 10
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: opening
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Open a pull request from a branch of the same repository or of a related
-- fork (head is a fork of base, base is a fork of the head owner's repository,
-- or both are forks of the same root). The web compare page pre-fills the
-- title from the single commit's summary (else the head branch name; longer
-- than max_title_length moves the rest into the description) and the
-- description from that commit's body followed by the repository's pull
-- request template.
-- from: services/pull/pull.go:40
rule UserOpensPullRequest {
    when: UserOpensPullRequest(user, base_repository, base_branch, head_repository, head_branch, title, body, allow_maintainer_edit)
    requires: base_repository.is_archived = false
    requires: base_repository.is_mirror = false
    requires: base_repository.is_empty = false
    requires: can_read_pulls(user, base_repository)
    requires: can_read_code(user, base_repository)
    requires: can_read_code(user, head_repository)
    requires: head_repository = base_repository or is_related_fork(head_repository, base_repository)
    requires: branch_exists(base_repository, base_branch)
    requires: branch_exists(head_repository, head_branch)
    requires: head_repository != base_repository or head_branch != base_branch
    requires: not is_blocked_by_owner(base_repository, user)
    requires: trimmed_length(title) > 0
    requires: not open_pull_request_exists(head_repository, head_branch, base_repository, base_branch)
    ensures:
        let conversation = issues/Issue.created(
            repository: base_repository,
            index: next_issue_index(base_repository),
            poster: user,
            title: truncate(title, config.max_title_length),
            content: body,
            content_version: 0,
            is_pull: true,
            status: open,
            is_locked: false,
            created_at: now,
            updated_at: now
        )
        let pr = PullRequest.created(
            issue: conversation,
            flow: branch,
            head_repository: head_repository,
            head_branch: head_branch,
            base_repository: base_repository,
            base_branch: base_branch,
            head_commit_sha: head_commit_of(head_repository, head_branch),
            created_at: now,
            status: checking,
            check_requested_at: now,
            conflicted_files: {},
            changed_protected_files: {},
            commits_ahead: commits_ahead_of(head_repository, head_branch, base_repository, base_branch),
            commits_behind: commits_behind_of(head_repository, head_branch, base_repository, base_branch),
            allow_maintainer_edit: allow_maintainer_edit
        )
        issues/Comment.created(issue: conversation, poster: user, kind: pull_push,
            content: commits_between(base_repository, base_branch, head_repository, head_branch),
            content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        PullRequestOpened(pull_request: pr)
    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /{owner}/{repo}/compare/{base}...{head} (CompareAndPullRequestPost);
        -- API: POST /repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls (head "branch" or "owner:branch").
        -- Labels, milestone, assignees, project and attachments chosen on the
        -- form are applied by issues/projects (writers only). The head commits
        -- are copied into the base repository's pull ref refs/pull/<index>/head.
        -- A pull request template is looked up at {"", .forgejo/, .gitea/,
        -- .github/, docs/}{PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE,pull_request_template}{.md,.yaml,.yml}
        -- on the default branch (YAML templates are issue forms).
        -- The compare page shows "nothing to compare" when head equals the
        -- merge base; an empty PR may still be opened unless the repository
        -- autodetects manual merges or head and base are the same branch.
}

-- CODEOWNERS: when a non-WIP pull request opens, owners of changed paths are
-- requested to review (by the poster).
-- from: services/issue/pull.go:28
rule CodeOwnersRequestedOnOpen {
    when: PullRequestOpened(pull_request)
    let pr = pull_request
    requires: not pr.is_work_in_progress
    ensures: CodeOwnerReviewRequestsDue(pull_request: pr)
}

-- A WIP prefix was removed from the title: the PR is ready for review and the
-- CODEOWNERS requests are made now.
-- from: services/issue/issue.go:90
rule PullRequestBecomesReadyForReview {
    when: issues/IssueTitleChanged(issue, doer, old_title)
    let pr = PullRequest{issue: issue}
    requires: exists pr
    requires: has_wip_prefix(old_title)
    requires: not pr.is_work_in_progress
    ensures: PullRequestReadyForReview(pull_request: pr, doer: doer)
    ensures: CodeOwnerReviewRequestsDue(pull_request: pr)
}

-- CODEOWNERS rules of the base repository's default branch request reviews
-- from the owners of every changed path (not for PRs into a fork).
-- from: services/issue/pull.go:72
rule RequestCodeOwnerReviews {
    when: CodeOwnerReviewRequestsDue(pull_request)
    let pr = pull_request
    requires: pr.base_repository.is_fork = false
    let rules = CodeOwnerRules where repository = pr.base_repository
    -- No CODEOWNERS file, no rules, nobody to request.
    requires: rules.count > 0
    let owners = code_owner_users(rules, pr)
    let owner_teams = code_owner_teams(rules, pr)
    let poster = pr.issue.poster
    ensures:
        for owner in owners:
            if owner != poster and can_read_pulls(owner, pr.base_repository)
                and not exists ReviewRequest{pull_request: pr, reviewer: owner}:
                ReviewRequest.created(pull_request: pr, reviewer: owner, team: null, requested_by: poster,
                    is_official: pr.is_official_reviewer(owner), created_at: now)
                ReviewRequested(pull_request: pr, requester: poster, reviewer: owner)
        for owner_team in owner_teams:
            if not exists ReviewRequest{pull_request: pr, team: owner_team}:
                ReviewRequest.created(pull_request: pr, reviewer: null, team: owner_team, requested_by: poster,
                    is_official: team_is_official_reviewer(owner_team, pr), created_at: now)
                TeamReviewRequested(pull_request: pr, requester: poster, team: owner_team)
    @guidance
        -- code_owner_users/teams: for every CodeOwnerRule and every path
        -- changed between the merge base and the head, a rule whose pattern
        -- matches (or, when negated, does not match) contributes its users and
        -- teams. Unknown users/teams are skipped (shown as warnings when
        -- viewing the CODEOWNERS file); a file larger than
        -- config.max_display_file_size is read truncated.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: AGit flow (push to refs/for/<base>[/<topic>])
------------------------------------------------------------

-- code accepted an AGit push for a topic with no open AGit PR: open one. The
-- head is the pushed commit, held only in the pull ref.
-- from: services/agit/agit.go:115
rule AgitPushOpensPullRequest {
    when: code/AgitPullRequestRequested(repository, pusher, base_branch, head_branch, head_sha, title, description)
    requires: can_read_pulls(pusher, repository)
    requires: not open_pull_request_exists(repository, head_branch, repository, base_branch)
    ensures:
        let conversation = issues/Issue.created(
            repository: repository,
            index: next_issue_index(repository),
            poster: pusher,
            title: truncate(title, config.max_title_length),
            content: description,
            content_version: 0,
            is_pull: true,
            status: open,
            is_locked: false,
            created_at: now,
            updated_at: now
        )
        let pr = PullRequest.created(
            issue: conversation,
            flow: agit,
            head_repository: repository,
            head_branch: head_branch,
            base_repository: repository,
            base_branch: base_branch,
            head_commit_sha: head_sha,
            created_at: now,
            status: checking,
            check_requested_at: now,
            conflicted_files: {},
            changed_protected_files: {},
            commits_ahead: 0,
            commits_behind: 0,
            allow_maintainer_edit: false
        )
        PullRequestOpened(pull_request: pr)
    @guidance
        -- Transport (code): `git push origin HEAD:refs/for/main -o topic=x
        -- [-o title=..] [-o description=..] [-o force-push=true]`, or
        -- refs/for/<base>/<topic>. The head branch is "<pusher>/<topic>".
        -- The push result reports refs/pull/<index>/head.
}

-- A further AGit push (to the topic, or to refs/pull/<index>/head by a code
-- writer or the poster) moves the PR head.
-- from: services/agit/agit.go:230
rule AgitPushUpdatesPullRequest {
    when: code/AgitPullRequestHeadPushed(pull, pusher, old_sha, new_sha)
    requires: pull.flow = agit
    requires: pull.is_open
    requires: can_write_code(pusher, pull.base_repository) or pusher = pull.issue.poster
    ensures: PullRequestHeadMoved(pull_request: pull, pusher: pusher, old_commit_sha: old_sha, new_commit_sha: new_sha)
}

-- AGit head branch names carry the poster's name; renaming the user renames them.
-- from: services/agit/agit.go:300
rule AgitHeadBranchesFollowPosterRename {
    when: accounts/UserRenamed(user, old_name, new_name)
    for pr in PullRequests where flow = agit and issue.poster = user and issue.status = open
            and (status = checking or status = mergeable or status = conflict or status = empty or status = ancestor or status = error):
        ensures: pr.head_branch = rename_agit_head_branch(pr.head_branch, old_name, new_name)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: head and base movement, mergeability checking
------------------------------------------------------------

-- `allium analyse` reports conflicts between the re-check rules (head/base
-- push, retarget, reopen, protection change) and the merge rules on the same
-- PullRequest state. They are real races between independent events and are
-- resolved by serialising work per pull request (Forgejo holds a per-PR lock
-- for check, merge, retarget and update): whichever runs second sees the
-- state the first left — a merge refuses a PR that went back to `checking`,
-- and a re-check of a PR already merged does nothing.

-- A push to a branch updates every open branch-flow PR using it as head.
-- from: services/pull/pull.go:298
rule HeadBranchPushUpdatesPullRequests {
    when: code/CommitsPushed(repository, branch_name, pusher, old_sha, new_sha, is_force)
    for pr in PullRequests where head_repository = repository and head_branch = branch_name
            and flow = branch and issue.status = open
            and (status = checking or status = mergeable or status = conflict or status = empty or status = ancestor or status = error)
            and head_commit_sha != new_sha:
        ensures: PullRequestHeadMoved(pull_request: pr, pusher: pusher, old_commit_sha: pr.head_commit_sha, new_commit_sha: new_sha)
    @guidance
        -- Only PRs that existed before the push was received are updated (a PR
        -- opened from the just-pushed commit is already current).
}

-- What happens whenever a PR's head moves (branch push, AGit push, update
-- branch, applied suggestion): the pull ref follows, the PR is re-checked,
-- reviews made against a different diff go stale (and approvals are dismissed
-- when the protection rule says so), code conversations whose lines changed
-- become outdated, and a push entry is added to the timeline.
-- from: services/pull/pull.go:378
rule PullRequestHeadMoves {
    when: PullRequestHeadMoved(pull_request, pusher, old_commit_sha, new_commit_sha)
    let pr = pull_request
    requires: (pr.status = checking or pr.status = mergeable or pr.status = conflict or pr.status = empty or pr.status = ancestor or pr.status = error)
    let diff_changed = diff_differs(pr, old_commit_sha, new_commit_sha)
    let dismiss = diff_changed and pr.protection != null and pr.protection.dismiss_stale_approvals
    let forced = is_force_push(pr.head_repository, old_commit_sha, new_commit_sha)
    ensures:
        pr.head_commit_sha = new_commit_sha
        pr.status = checking
        pr.check_requested_at = now
        pr.commits_ahead = commits_ahead_of(pr.head_repository, pr.head_branch, pr.base_repository, pr.base_branch)
        pr.commits_behind = commits_behind_of(pr.head_repository, pr.head_branch, pr.base_repository, pr.base_branch)
        for review in Reviews where pull_request = pr and status = submitted:
            if review.commit_sha = new_commit_sha:
                review.is_stale = false
            else if diff_changed:
                review.is_stale = true
        for approval in Reviews where pull_request = pr and status = submitted and kind = approve and is_official = true and is_dismissed = false:
            if dismiss:
                approval.is_dismissed = true
                ReviewDismissed(review: approval, dismisser: pusher, message: "New commits pushed, approval review dismissed automatically according to repository settings")
        for conversation in CodeConversations where pull_request = pr and is_outdated = false:
            if anchored_lines_changed(conversation, new_commit_sha):
                conversation.is_outdated = true
        issues/Comment.created(issue: pr.issue, poster: pusher, kind: pull_push,
            content: commits_between_shas(pr.base_repository, old_commit_sha, new_commit_sha),
            content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        PullRequestHeadUpdated(pull_request: pr, pusher: pusher, old_commit_sha: old_commit_sha, new_commit_sha: new_commit_sha, is_force_push: forced)
        PullRequestSynchronized(pull_request: pr, doer: pusher)
    @guidance
        -- "Diff differs" compares the diff of old head vs base with new head vs
        -- base (a rebase that keeps the same changes does not make reviews
        -- stale). The push entry lists the new commit ids, or marks a force
        -- push with old..new. Forgejo skips the outdating step for AGit pushes;
        -- a rebuild should not.
}

-- A push to a branch re-checks every open PR that targets it.
-- from: services/pull/pull.go:357
rule BaseBranchPushRechecksPullRequests {
    when: code/CommitsPushed(repository, branch_name, pusher, old_sha, new_sha, is_force)
    for pr in PullRequests where base_repository = repository and base_branch = branch_name and issue.status = open
            and (status = checking or status = mergeable or status = conflict or status = empty or status = ancestor or status = error):
        ensures: pr.status = checking
        ensures: pr.check_requested_at = now
        ensures: pr.commits_ahead = commits_ahead_of(pr.head_repository, pr.head_branch, pr.base_repository, pr.base_branch)
        ensures: pr.commits_behind = commits_behind_of(pr.head_repository, pr.head_branch, pr.base_repository, pr.base_branch)
}

-- Changing a branch protection rule re-checks PRs into matching branches
-- (protected-file changes and status-check requirements may differ).
-- from: services/pull/check.go:339
rule ProtectionChangeRechecksPullRequests {
    when: code/BranchProtectionChanged(rule)
    for pr in PullRequests where base_repository = rule.repository and issue.status = open
            and (status = checking or status = mergeable or status = conflict or status = empty or status = ancestor or status = error)
            and rule_matches_branch(rule, base_branch):
        ensures: pr.status = checking
        ensures: pr.check_requested_at = now
}

-- The asynchronous mergeability check. Records the merge base, conflicting
-- files and protected files changed; detects a PR already merged outside
-- Forgejo when the repository autodetects manual merges.
-- from: services/pull/check.go:302
rule CheckMergeability {
    when: pr: PullRequest.check_requested_at <= now
    requires: pr.status = checking
    let outcome = merge_check_outcome(pr)
    ensures:
        pr.check_requested_at = null
        pr.last_check_outcome = outcome
        pr.merge_base_sha = merge_base_of(pr)
        if outcome = failed:
            pr.status = error
        else if outcome = already_in_base and autodetects_manual_merge(pr.base_repository):
            pr.status = manually_merged
            pr.merge_style = manually_merged
            pr.merged_commit_sha = merge_commit_containing(pr)
            pr.merged_at = commit_authored_at(pr.base_repository, merge_commit_containing(pr))
            pr.merger = manual_merge_author(pr)
            pr.conflicted_files = {}
            pr.merged_automatically = false
            PullRequestMerged(pull_request: pr, merger: manual_merge_author(pr))
        else if outcome = already_in_base:
            pr.status = ancestor
        else if outcome = conflicting:
            pr.status = conflict
            pr.conflicted_files = conflicting_files(pr)
        else if outcome = no_changes:
            pr.status = empty
            pr.conflicted_files = {}
            pr.changed_protected_files = {}
        else:
            pr.status = mergeable
            pr.conflicted_files = {}
            pr.changed_protected_files = protected_files_changed(pr)
    @guidance
        -- manual_merge_author: the user whose email authored the merge commit,
        -- else the base repository owner. merge_commit_containing: the first
        -- merge commit on the ancestry path head..base, else the head commit
        -- (fast-forward). Conflicts honour settings.ignore_whitespace_conflicts.
        -- protected_files_changed: changed paths matching the protection rule's
        -- protected_file_patterns (case-insensitive globs), at most
        -- config.max_reported_protected_files. A newer re-check request
        -- supersedes an in-flight one.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: editing the proposal
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: services/pull/pull.go:168
rule UserChangesPullRequestTarget {
    when: UserChangesPullRequestTarget(user, pr, new_base_branch)
    requires: pr.base_repository.is_archived = false
    requires: pr.may_manage(user)
    requires: pr.is_open
    requires: (pr.status = checking or pr.status = mergeable or pr.status = conflict or pr.status = empty or pr.status = ancestor or pr.status = error)
    requires: new_base_branch != pr.base_branch
    requires: branch_exists(pr.base_repository, new_base_branch)
    requires: not head_equals_branch(pr, new_base_branch)
    requires: not open_pull_request_exists(pr.head_repository, pr.head_branch, pr.base_repository, new_base_branch)
    ensures:
        pr.base_branch = new_base_branch
        pr.status = checking
        pr.check_requested_at = now
        pr.commits_ahead = commits_ahead_of(pr.head_repository, pr.head_branch, pr.base_repository, new_base_branch)
        pr.commits_behind = commits_behind_of(pr.head_repository, pr.head_branch, pr.base_repository, new_base_branch)
        issues/Comment.created(issue: pr.issue, poster: user, kind: change_target_branch, content: "",
            old_ref: pr.base_branch, new_ref: new_base_branch,
            content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        PullRequestTargetBranchChanged(pull_request: pr, doer: user, old_base_branch: pr.base_branch)
    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /{owner}/{repo}/pull/{index}/target_branch; API: PATCH
        -- /repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/{index} with `base`.
}

-- Only the poster, and only while they can write the head repository, may
-- toggle "allow edits from maintainers".
-- from: services/pull/edits.go:64
rule AuthorSetsMaintainerEdits {
    when: AuthorSetsMaintainerEdits(user, pr, allow)
    requires: user = pr.issue.poster
    requires: can_write_code(user, pr.head_repository)
    ensures: pr.allow_maintainer_edit = allow
    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /pulls/{index}/set_allow_maintainer_edit; API: PATCH
        -- pulls/{index} `allow_maintainer_edit`. Maintainers granted this way
        -- may push to the head branch (web editor, update branch, apply
        -- suggestion) but not delete it.
}

-- Renaming a branch carries every unmerged PR (open or closed) with it, as
-- head and as base.
-- from: models/git/branch.go:395
rule BranchRenameCarriesPullRequests {
    when: code/BranchRenamed(repository, from_name, to_name, by)
    ensures:
        for pr in PullRequests:
            if pr.base_repository = repository and pr.base_branch = from_name and pr.status != merged and pr.status != manually_merged:
                pr.base_branch = to_name
            if pr.head_repository = repository and pr.head_branch = from_name and pr.flow = branch and pr.status != merged and pr.status != manually_merged:
                pr.head_branch = to_name
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: closing and reopening
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The poster or a pull-request writer closes. Open dependencies block closing.
-- from: routers/web/repo/issue.go:3171
rule UserClosesPullRequest {
    when: UserClosesPullRequest(user, pr)
    requires: pr.base_repository.is_archived = false
    requires: pr.may_manage(user)
    requires: pr.is_open
    requires: not pr.is_merged
    requires: not is_blocked_by_owner(pr.base_repository, user)
    requires: not has_open_blocking_dependencies(pr.issue)
    ensures: pr.issue.status = closed
    ensures: pr.issue.closed_at = now
    ensures: issues/Comment.created(issue: pr.issue, poster: user, kind: close, content: "",
        content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
    ensures: PullRequestClosed(pull_request: pr, doer: user)
    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /issues/{index}/comments with status=close; API: PATCH
        -- pulls/{index} state=closed. A scheduled auto-merge stays recorded but
        -- cannot fire while closed (see open question). The closer's stopwatch
        -- stops (issues).
}

-- Reopening re-copies the head into the pull ref when they diverged and queues
-- a fresh check. Refused for merged PRs, when another open PR has the same
-- head and base, or (branch flow) when the head or base branch is gone.
-- from: routers/web/repo/issue.go:3178
rule UserReopensPullRequest {
    when: UserReopensPullRequest(user, pr)
    requires: pr.base_repository.is_archived = false
    requires: pr.may_manage(user)
    requires: pr.issue.status = closed
    requires: (pr.status = checking or pr.status = mergeable or pr.status = conflict or pr.status = empty or pr.status = ancestor or pr.status = error)
    requires: not open_pull_request_exists(pr.head_repository, pr.head_branch, pr.base_repository, pr.base_branch)
    requires: pr.flow = agit or (pr.base_branch_present and pr.head_branch_present)
    requires: not is_blocked_by_owner(pr.base_repository, user)
    ensures:
        pr.issue.status = open
        pr.issue.closed_at = null
        pr.status = checking
        pr.check_requested_at = now
        if pr.flow = branch:
            pr.head_commit_sha = head_commit_of(pr.head_repository, pr.head_branch)
        issues/Comment.created(issue: pr.issue, poster: user, kind: reopen, content: "",
            content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        PullRequestReopened(pull_request: pr, doer: user)
}

-- Deleting a branch closes the open PRs that use it as head or base (after any
-- retargeting done by a merge cleanup).
-- from: services/pull/pull.go:527
rule DeletedBranchClosesPullRequests {
    when: code/BranchDeleted(branch, by)
    for pr in PullRequests where issue.status = open
            and (status = checking or status = mergeable or status = conflict or status = empty or status = ancestor or status = error)
            and ((head_repository = branch.repository and head_branch = branch.name and flow != agit)
                 or (base_repository = branch.repository and base_branch = branch.name)):
        ensures: pr.issue.status = closed
        ensures: pr.issue.closed_at = now
        ensures: issues/Comment.created(issue: pr.issue, poster: by, kind: close, content: "",
            content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        ensures: PullRequestClosed(pull_request: pr, doer: by)
}

-- Deleting a repository closes open PRs from its branches into other repositories.
-- from: services/pull/pull.go:556
rule DeletedRepositoryClosesOutgoingPullRequests {
    when: repositories/RepositoryDeleted(repository, doer)
    for pr in PullRequests where head_repository = repository and base_repository != repository and issue.status = open
            and (status = checking or status = mergeable or status = conflict or status = empty or status = ancestor or status = error):
        ensures: pr.issue.status = closed
        ensures: pr.issue.closed_at = now
        ensures: PullRequestClosed(pull_request: pr, doer: doer)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: updating the head from the base
------------------------------------------------------------

-- "Update branch": bring base commits into the head by a merge commit
-- ("Merge branch '<base>' into <head>") or by rebasing the head onto base and
-- force-pushing it. Not available for AGit PRs.
-- from: services/pull/update.go:25
rule UserUpdatesPullRequestBranch {
    when: UserUpdatesPullRequestBranch(user, pr, style)
    requires: pr.is_open
    requires: not pr.is_merged
    requires: pr.flow = branch
    requires: pr.commits_behind > 0
    requires: (style = merge and may_update_by_merge(user, pr)) or (style = rebase and may_update_by_rebase(user, pr))
    requires: within_quota(pr.head_repository)
    ensures: PullRequestHeadMoved(pull_request: pr, pusher: user, old_commit_sha: pr.head_commit_sha, new_commit_sha: updated_head(pr, style))
    ensures: PullRequestBranchUpdated(pull_request: pr, doer: user, style: style)
    @guidance
        -- may_update_by_merge: the user may "merge into" the head branch (code
        -- writer of the head repository, or the head branch protection's merge
        -- allowlist), or — when maintainer edits are allowed — the same test
        -- with their base-repository permission; when the head branch is
        -- protected they must also be allowed to push to it.
        -- may_update_by_rebase: as above, plus the head branch is NOT
        -- protected (a rebase needs a force push) and the head repository's
        -- pull-request settings allow_rebase_update. Conflicts abort with the
        -- conflicting output; nothing changes.
        -- Web: POST /pulls/{index}/update?style=merge|rebase; API: POST
        -- /repos/{o}/{r}/pulls/{index}/update?style=merge|rebase. The UI
        -- default is the repository's default_update_style, else
        -- config.default_update_style.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: merging
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Merge now. Composes the commit message from the template (or the default
-- message) unless the merger typed one; the merge is pushed to the base branch
-- as the merger, then the PR is marked merged (issues then closes its
-- conversation and applies closing keywords).
-- from: services/pull/check.go:68
rule UserMergesPullRequest {
    when: UserMergesPullRequest(user, pr, style, title, message, expected_head_sha, delete_branch_after_merge, force_merge)
    requires: pr.base_repository.is_archived = false
    requires: style != manually_merged
    requires: pr.allows_style(style)
    requires: pr.is_open
    requires: pr.may_merge(user)
    requires: not pr.is_work_in_progress
    requires: pr.status = mergeable or pr.status = empty
    requires: pr.protection_satisfied or (force_merge and pr.may_bypass_protection(user))
    requires: merge_signing_satisfied(pr, user, style)
    requires: not has_open_blocking_dependencies(pr.issue)
    requires: expected_head_sha = null or expected_head_sha = pr.head_commit_sha
    requires: pr.head_branch_present
    requires: within_quota(pr.base_repository)
    let final_message = compose_merge_message(pr, style, title, message)
    ensures:
        pr.status = merged
        pr.merge_style = style
        pr.merged_commit_sha = merge_result_commit(pr, style, final_message)
        pr.merger = user
        pr.merged_at = now
        pr.check_requested_at = null
        pr.conflicted_files = {}
        not exists pr.auto_merge
        pr.merged_automatically = false
        PullRequestMerged(pull_request: pr, merger: user)
        if delete_branch_after_merge:
            PullRequestHeadBranchDeletionRequested(pull_request: pr, doer: user)
    @guidance
        -- Styles: merge = merge commit; rebase = rebase head onto base then
        -- fast-forward (amending the last commit only if a REBASE template
        -- exists); rebase_merge = rebase then --no-ff merge commit; squash = one
        -- commit authored by the poster (using the poster's own commit identity
        -- when one of the PR's commits has it) with Co-authored-by trailers;
        -- fast_forward_only = fails unless base can fast-forward to head.
        -- Failures that leave the PR unmerged: merge/rebase conflicts, unrelated
        -- histories, base moved during the merge, head moved since the merger
        -- loaded the page (expected_head_sha), push rejected by hooks (the
        -- merge push is a code/Push with merging_pull set; its pre-receive
        -- re-checks may_merge and protection except protected files).
        -- Web: POST /{o}/{r}/pulls/{index}/merge (form fields do,
        -- merge_title_field, merge_message_field, head_commit_id,
        -- delete_branch_after_merge, force_merge, merge_when_checks_succeed);
        -- API: POST /repos/{o}/{r}/pulls/{index}/merge; GET .../merge answers
        -- whether merged.
        -- Message composition (compose_merge_message / default_merge_message):
        -- a typed title replaces the template/default title and a typed body is
        -- appended after a blank line.
        -- Template lookup per style: .forgejo/default_merge_message/<STYLE>_TEMPLATE.md,
        -- then .gitea/..., on the default branch (read up to
        -- config.default_merge_message_size), then an instance-level
        -- custom/default_merge_message/<STYLE>_TEMPLATE.md. First line = title,
        -- rest = body; empty parts fall back to the defaults. Variables:
        -- BaseRepoOwnerName, BaseRepoName, BaseBranch, HeadRepoOwnerName,
        -- HeadRepoName, HeadBranch, PullRequestTitle, PullRequestDescription,
        -- PullRequestPosterName, PullRequestIndex, PullRequestReference,
        -- ReviewedOn, ReviewedBy, ClosingIssues.
        -- Defaults: squash "<title> (#<index>)"; others "Merge pull request
        -- '<title>' (#<index>) from <head> into <base>" ("!" instead of "#"
        -- with an external tracker). Body: "Reviewed-on: <url>" then up to
        -- config.default_merge_message_max_approvers "Reviewed-by:" lines
        -- (official approvers only when configured). Squash bodies start with
        -- the PR description (or the commit messages, up to
        -- default_merge_message_size, when
        -- populate_squash_comment_with_commit_messages) then Co-authored-by
        -- lines for other authors among the first
        -- default_merge_message_commits_limit commits (all commits with
        -- default_merge_message_all_authors).
}

-- Whatever way a pull request got merged, each issue it references with a
-- closing or reopening keyword (title, description or its comments) is closed
-- or reopened by the merger; issues applies the change (and leaves an issue
-- with open blockers open).
-- from: services/pull/merge.go:288
rule MergeResolvesReferencedIssues {
    when: PullRequestMerged(pull_request, merger)
    ensures:
        for target in issues_closed_by(pull_request):
            IssueClosedByPullRequest(issue: target, pull_request: pull_request, doer: merger)
        for target in issues_reopened_by(pull_request):
            IssueReopenedByPullRequest(issue: target, pull_request: pull_request, doer: merger)
}

-- The merge push reached the base branch (code's post-receive). Marks the PR
-- merged when the merge rule has not already done so.
-- from: routers/private/hook_post_receive.go:355
rule MergePushMarksPullRequestMerged {
    when: code/MergePushCompleted(pull, pusher, merge_commit_sha)
    requires: (pull.status = mergeable or pull.status = empty)
    ensures:
        pull.status = merged
        pull.merge_style = merge
        pull.merged_commit_sha = merge_commit_sha
        pull.merger = pusher
        pull.merged_at = now
        pull.check_requested_at = null
        pull.conflicted_files = {}
        not exists pull.auto_merge
        pull.merged_automatically = false
        PullRequestMerged(pull_request: pull, merger: pusher)
    @guidance
        -- In a rebuild where UserMergesPullRequest records the merge directly
        -- this rule never finds an unmerged PR; it exists for the git-transport
        -- path, where the merge is a push carrying merging_pull. The style is
        -- the one the merge was started with.
}

-- Mark as merged when the commits already reached the base branch outside
-- Forgejo. Requires only merge permission and the repository setting; the
-- commit must exist and be contained in the base branch.
-- from: services/pull/merge_manual.go:24
rule UserMarksPullRequestManuallyMerged {
    when: UserMarksPullRequestManuallyMerged(user, pr, commit_sha)
    requires: pr.base_repository.is_archived = false
    requires: (pr.status = checking or pr.status = mergeable or pr.status = conflict or pr.status = empty or pr.status = ancestor or pr.status = error)
    requires: pr.is_open
    requires: pr.may_merge(user)
    requires: pr.allows_style(manually_merged)
    requires: commit_in_branch(pr.base_repository, pr.base_branch, commit_sha)
    ensures:
        pr.status = manually_merged
        pr.merge_style = manually_merged
        pr.merged_commit_sha = full_commit_sha(pr.base_repository, commit_sha)
        pr.merged_at = commit_authored_at(pr.base_repository, commit_sha)
        pr.merger = user
        pr.check_requested_at = null
        pr.conflicted_files = {}
        pr.merged_automatically = false
        PullRequestMerged(pull_request: pr, merger: user)
    @guidance
        -- Accepts full or abbreviated ids in any case; an ambiguous or
        -- unknown id is "wrong commit ID". Same endpoints as merge with
        -- do=manually-merged and merge_commit_id.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: auto-merge ("merge when checks succeed")
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Scheduling runs the same checks as merging except that unmet branch
-- protection (status checks, approvals, ...) does not refuse it.
-- from: services/automerge/automerge.go:56
rule UserSchedulesAutoMerge {
    when: UserSchedulesAutoMerge(user, pr, style, message, delete_branch_after_merge)
    requires: pr.base_repository.is_archived = false
    requires: style != manually_merged
    requires: pr.allows_style(style)
    requires: not pr.is_merged
    requires: pr.is_open
    requires: pr.may_merge(user)
    requires: not pr.is_work_in_progress
    requires: pr.status = mergeable or pr.status = empty
    requires: merge_signing_satisfied(pr, user, style)
    requires: not has_open_blocking_dependencies(pr.issue)
    requires: not exists pr.auto_merge
    ensures: AutoMerge.created(pull_request: pr, scheduled_by: user, style: style,
        message: message ?? default_merge_message(pr, style),
        delete_branch_after_merge: delete_branch_after_merge, created_at: now)
    ensures: issues/Comment.created(issue: pr.issue, poster: user, kind: pull_scheduled_merge, content: "",
        content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
    ensures: AutoMergeScheduled(pull_request: pr, doer: user)
    @guidance
        -- Web: merge form with merge_when_checks_succeed=true (replaces an
        -- existing schedule); API: same field on POST pulls/{index}/merge
        -- (refuses when one exists).
}

-- from: services/automerge/automerge.go:70
rule UserCancelsAutoMerge {
    when: UserCancelsAutoMerge(user, pr)
    requires: pr.base_repository.is_archived = false
    requires: exists pr.auto_merge
    requires: user = pr.auto_merge.scheduled_by or pr.may_merge(user)
    ensures: not exists pr.auto_merge
    ensures: issues/Comment.created(issue: pr.issue, poster: user, kind: pull_cancel_scheduled_merge, content: "",
        content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
    ensures: AutoMergeCancelled(pull_request: pr, doer: user)
    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /pulls/{index}/cancel_auto_merge; API: DELETE pulls/{index}/merge.
}

-- When a scheduled PR becomes mergeable with passing required checks, it is
-- merged as the scheduler — provided they may still merge and every merge
-- precondition, including branch protection, now holds. Otherwise it stays
-- scheduled and is re-evaluated on the next status, review or check event.
-- from: services/automerge/automerge.go:116
rule AutoMergeExecutes {
    when: scheduled: AutoMerge.is_ready
    let pr = scheduled.pull_request
    requires: pr.status = mergeable
    requires: pr.may_merge(scheduled.scheduled_by)
    requires: pr.allows_style(scheduled.style)
    requires: not pr.is_work_in_progress
    requires: pr.protection_satisfied
    requires: merge_signing_satisfied(pr, scheduled.scheduled_by, scheduled.style)
    requires: not has_open_blocking_dependencies(pr.issue)
    ensures:
        pr.status = merged
        pr.merge_style = scheduled.style
        pr.merged_commit_sha = merge_result_commit(pr, scheduled.style, scheduled.message)
        pr.merger = scheduled.scheduled_by
        pr.merged_at = now
        pr.check_requested_at = null
        pr.conflicted_files = {}
        pr.merged_automatically = true
        PullRequestAutoMerged(pull_request: pr, merger: scheduled.scheduled_by)
        PullRequestMerged(pull_request: pr, merger: scheduled.scheduled_by)
        if scheduled.delete_branch_after_merge:
            PullRequestHeadBranchDeletionRequested(pull_request: pr, doer: scheduled.scheduled_by)
        -- the schedule is removed last: everything above reads it
        not exists scheduled
    @guidance
        -- Triggered in Forgejo by: a commit status on the head commit
        -- (code/CommitStatusCreated), an approval, a dismissed review, and a
        -- check finishing as mergeable. The head commit must still be the one
        -- the triggering event was about. A failing merge is only logged (see
        -- open question).
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: head branch cleanup and retargeting
------------------------------------------------------------

-- "Delete branch" on a merged or closed PR, offered when the branch has no
-- commits beyond the PR head.
-- from: routers/web/repo/pull.go:1751
rule UserDeletesPullRequestHeadBranch {
    when: UserDeletesPullRequestHeadBranch(user, pr)
    requires: pr.is_merged or pr.issue.status = closed
    requires: pr.flow = branch
    requires: head_commit_of(pr.head_repository, pr.head_branch) = pr.head_commit_sha
    ensures: PullRequestHeadBranchDeletionRequested(pull_request: pr, doer: user)
}

-- Deleting the head branch after a merge: no other open PR may use it as head
-- and the deleter must write the head repository (maintainer edits do not
-- grant deletion). Children (open PRs in the same repository targeting this
-- head branch) are first retargeted to this PR's base, then code deletes the
-- branch (refusing the default branch and protected branches).
-- from: services/repository/branch.go:502
rule DeletePullRequestHeadBranch {
    when: PullRequestHeadBranchDeletionRequested(pull_request, doer)
    let pr = pull_request
    let user = doer
    let head = code/Branch{repository: pr.head_repository, name: pr.head_branch, status: live}
    requires: exists head
    requires: not has_other_open_pull_request_from(pr)
    requires: can_write_code(user, pr.head_repository)
    ensures:
        if config.retarget_children_on_merge and pr.is_merged and pr.head_repository = pr.base_repository:
            for child in open_pull_requests_into(pr.head_repository, pr.head_branch):
                if (child.status = checking or child.status = mergeable or child.status = conflict or child.status = empty or child.status = ancestor or child.status = error):
                    child.base_branch = pr.base_branch
                    child.status = checking
                    child.check_requested_at = now
                    issues/Comment.created(issue: child.issue, poster: user, kind: change_target_branch, content: "",
                        old_ref: pr.head_branch, new_ref: pr.base_branch,
                        content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
                    PullRequestTargetBranchChanged(pull_request: child, doer: user, old_base_branch: pr.head_branch)
        HeadBranchDeletionRequested(user: user, branch: head)
        issues/Comment.created(issue: pr.issue, poster: user, kind: delete_branch, content: "",
            old_ref: pr.head_branch, content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        PullRequestHeadBranchDeleted(pull_request: pr, doer: user)
    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /pulls/{index}/cleanup, or delete_branch_after_merge on the
        -- merge form / schedule. A refusal after a successful merge is
        -- reported but does not undo the merge. Retargeting skips children
        -- that would duplicate an open PR.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: reviews
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Add a code comment to the user's pending review (creating the pending review
-- at the current head if there is none). Only the author sees it until the
-- review is submitted.
-- from: services/pull/review.go:131
rule UserAddsPendingCodeComment {
    when: UserAddsPendingCodeComment(user, pr, path, line, side, extra_lines, body)
    let draft = Review{pull_request: pr, reviewer: user, status: pending}
    requires: exists draft
    requires: pr.base_repository.is_archived = false
    requires: can_read_pulls(user, pr.base_repository)
    requires: not pr.issue.is_locked or can_write_pulls(user, pr.base_repository)
    requires: extra_lines >= 0
    requires: config.max_code_comment_lines = 0 or extra_lines + 1 <= config.max_code_comment_lines
    requires: count_suggestions(body) <= 1
    ensures:
        let thread = CodeConversation.created(pull_request: pr, review: draft, path: path, line: line, side: side,
            extra_lines: extra_lines, commit_sha: blamed_commit(pr, path, line, side),
            diff_hunk: diff_hunk_around(pr, path, line, side, extra_lines),
            is_outdated: false, resolved_by: null)
        ReviewComment.created(conversation: thread, review: draft, poster: user, body: body, created_at: now)
    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /pulls/{index}/files/reviews/comments (side=previous|proposed,
        -- line, extra_lines_count, tree_path, before_commit_id, latest_commit_id);
        -- API: comments inside POST pulls/{index}/reviews with event PENDING, or
        -- POST pulls/{index}/reviews/{id}/comments. The anchor is the blame of
        -- the line on the commit being viewed; comments on removed lines stay
        -- on the previous side.
}

-- The first pending code comment starts the user's draft review at the
-- current head.
-- from: services/pull/review.go:183
rule UserStartsDraftReview {
    when: UserAddsPendingCodeComment(user, pr, path, line, side, extra_lines, body)
    let draft = Review{pull_request: pr, reviewer: user, status: pending}
    requires: not exists draft
    requires: pr.base_repository.is_archived = false
    requires: can_read_pulls(user, pr.base_repository)
    requires: not pr.issue.is_locked or can_write_pulls(user, pr.base_repository)
    requires: extra_lines >= 0
    requires: config.max_code_comment_lines = 0 or extra_lines + 1 <= config.max_code_comment_lines
    requires: count_suggestions(body) <= 1
    ensures:
        let new_draft = Review.created(pull_request: pr, reviewer: user, status: pending, body: "",
            commit_sha: pr.head_commit_sha, is_official: false, is_stale: false, is_dismissed: false, created_at: now)
        let new_thread = CodeConversation.created(pull_request: pr, review: new_draft, path: path, line: line, side: side,
            extra_lines: extra_lines, commit_sha: blamed_commit(pr, path, line, side),
            diff_hunk: diff_hunk_around(pr, path, line, side, extra_lines),
            is_outdated: false, resolved_by: null)
        ReviewComment.created(conversation: new_thread, review: new_draft, poster: user, body: body, created_at: now)
}

-- "Add single comment": a code comment published at once as a `comment` review.
-- from: services/pull/review.go:204
rule UserPostsSingleCodeComment {
    when: UserPostsSingleCodeComment(user, pr, path, line, side, extra_lines, body)
    requires: pr.base_repository.is_archived = false
    requires: can_read_pulls(user, pr.base_repository)
    requires: not pr.issue.is_locked or can_write_pulls(user, pr.base_repository)
    requires: extra_lines >= 0
    requires: config.max_code_comment_lines = 0 or extra_lines + 1 <= config.max_code_comment_lines
    requires: count_suggestions(body) <= 1
    requires: trimmed_length(body) > 0
    ensures:
        let single = Review.created(pull_request: pr, reviewer: user, status: submitted, kind: comment, body: "",
            commit_sha: pr.head_commit_sha, is_official: false, is_stale: false, is_dismissed: false,
            created_at: now, submitted_at: now)
        let thread = CodeConversation.created(pull_request: pr, review: single, path: path, line: line, side: side,
            extra_lines: extra_lines, commit_sha: blamed_commit(pr, path, line, side), diff_hunk: diff_hunk_around(pr, path, line, side, extra_lines),
            is_outdated: false, resolved_by: null)
        let posted = ReviewComment.created(conversation: thread, review: single, poster: user, body: body, created_at: now)
        ReviewSubmitted(review: single)
        PullRequestCodeCommented(pull_request: pr, comment: posted)
}

-- Replying to a conversation: joins the thread. A reply to one's own pending
-- review stays pending; any other reply is visible immediately.
-- from: services/pull/review.go:160
rule UserRepliesToCodeConversation {
    when: UserRepliesToCodeConversation(user, pr, thread, body)
    requires: thread.pull_request = pr
    requires: pr.base_repository.is_archived = false
    requires: can_read_pulls(user, pr.base_repository)
    requires: not pr.issue.is_locked or can_write_pulls(user, pr.base_repository)
    requires: thread.review.status = submitted or thread.review.reviewer = user
    requires: trimmed_length(body) > 0
    requires: count_suggestions(body) <= 1
    ensures:
        let reply = ReviewComment.created(conversation: thread, review: thread.review, poster: user, body: body, created_at: now)
        if thread.review.status = submitted:
            PullRequestCodeCommented(pull_request: pr, comment: reply)
}

-- from: routers/api/v1/repo/pull_review.go:1066
rule UserEditsReviewComment {
    when: UserEditsReviewComment(user, pr, comment, body)
    requires: comment.conversation.pull_request = pr
    requires: pr.base_repository.is_archived = false
    requires: user = comment.poster or can_write_pulls(user, pr.base_repository)
    requires: not pr.issue.is_locked or can_write_pulls(user, pr.base_repository)
    requires: count_suggestions(body) <= 1
    ensures: comment.body = body
}

-- Deleting the last comment of a pending review removes the pending review.
-- from: services/issue/comments.go:121
rule UserDeletesReviewComment {
    when: UserDeletesReviewComment(user, pr, comment)
    requires: comment.conversation.pull_request = pr
    requires: pr.base_repository.is_archived = false
    requires: user = comment.poster or can_write_pulls(user, pr.base_repository)
    ensures:
        not exists comment
        if comment.conversation.comments.count <= 1:
            not exists comment.conversation
        if comment.review.status = pending and comment.review.comments.count <= 1:
            not exists comment.review
}

-- Submit a review: the pending review (if any) becomes the submitted review,
-- else a new one is created. Approve / request changes:
--   * may not be given by the PR poster;
--   * the reviewer's earlier reviews lose `is_official`, the new one is official
--     when the reviewer is an official reviewer;
--   * the reviewer's earlier approve/request_changes reviews are superseded
--     (marked dismissed) so they cannot resurface;
--   * team review requests of teams the reviewer belongs to are fulfilled
--     (organization-owned repositories).
-- Any verdict fulfils the reviewer's own review request. `comment` (and
-- request_changes) need a body or code comments.
-- from: models/issues/review.go:350
rule UserSubmitsDraftReview {
    when: UserSubmitsDraftReview(user, draft, verdict, body, commit_sha)
    let pr = draft.pull_request
    let decisive = verdict = approve or verdict = request_changes
    requires: draft.reviewer = user
    requires: draft.status = pending
    requires: pr.base_repository.is_archived = false
    requires: can_read_pulls(user, pr.base_repository)
    requires: not (decisive and user = pr.issue.poster)
    requires: verdict = approve or trimmed_length(body) > 0 or draft.comments.count > 0
    let official = decisive and pr.is_official_reviewer(user)
    let stale = decisive and commit_sha != pr.head_commit_sha and diff_differs(pr, commit_sha, pr.head_commit_sha)
    ensures:
        for earlier in Reviews where pull_request = pr and reviewer = user and status = submitted:
            if decisive:
                earlier.is_official = false
                if earlier.is_blocking_verdict:
                    earlier.is_dismissed = true
        draft.status = submitted
        draft.kind = verdict
        draft.body = body
        draft.commit_sha = commit_sha
        draft.is_official = official
        draft.is_stale = stale
        draft.submitted_at = now
        ReviewVerdictRecorded(pull_request: pr, verdict_review: draft, author: user, decisive: decisive)
    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /pulls/{index}/files/reviews/submit (type approve|comment|reject);
        -- API: POST pulls/{index}/reviews (event APPROVED|REQUEST_CHANGES|COMMENT|PENDING,
        -- body, commit_id, comments[]) and POST pulls/{index}/reviews/{id} to submit
        -- a pending one. Code comments of the review are published with it
        -- (PullRequestCodeCommented per comment). An approval re-evaluates auto-merge.
        -- The web form submits the user's pending draft when one exists
        -- (UserSubmitsDraftReview) and creates a review otherwise
        -- (UserSubmitsReview).
}

-- Submitting without a draft creates the submitted review directly.
-- from: models/issues/review.go:376
rule UserSubmitsReview {
    when: UserSubmitsReview(user, pr, verdict, body, commit_sha)
    let draft = Review{pull_request: pr, reviewer: user, status: pending}
    let decisive = verdict = approve or verdict = request_changes
    requires: not exists draft
    requires: pr.base_repository.is_archived = false
    requires: can_read_pulls(user, pr.base_repository)
    requires: not (decisive and user = pr.issue.poster)
    requires: verdict = approve or trimmed_length(body) > 0
    let official = decisive and pr.is_official_reviewer(user)
    let stale = decisive and commit_sha != pr.head_commit_sha and diff_differs(pr, commit_sha, pr.head_commit_sha)
    ensures:
        for earlier in Reviews where pull_request = pr and reviewer = user and status = submitted:
            if decisive:
                earlier.is_official = false
                if earlier.is_blocking_verdict:
                    earlier.is_dismissed = true
        let submitted = Review.created(pull_request: pr, reviewer: user, status: submitted, kind: verdict, body: body,
            commit_sha: commit_sha, is_official: official, is_stale: stale, is_dismissed: false,
            created_at: now, submitted_at: now)
        ReviewVerdictRecorded(pull_request: pr, verdict_review: submitted, author: user, decisive: decisive)
}

-- What every submitted verdict does to pending review requests (the
-- submitting rules already made the reviewer's earlier reviews unofficial and
-- superseded — marked dismissed — their earlier approve/request_changes
-- reviews when the new verdict is decisive):
--   * any verdict fulfils the reviewer's own review request;
--   * approve / request changes fulfil requests of teams the reviewer belongs
--     to (organization-owned repositories).
-- from: models/issues/review.go:286
rule ReviewVerdictSupersedesEarlierState {
    when: ReviewVerdictRecorded(pull_request, verdict_review, author, decisive)
    let pr = pull_request
    ensures:
        for request in ReviewRequests where pull_request = pr and reviewer = author:
            not exists request
        for team_request in ReviewRequests where pull_request = pr and team != null:
            if decisive and is_team_member(author, team_request.team) and is_organization_owned(pr.base_repository):
                not exists team_request
        issues/Comment.created(issue: pr.issue, poster: author, kind: review, content: verdict_review.body, review: verdict_review,
            content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        ReviewSubmitted(review: verdict_review)
        for remark in ReviewComments where review = verdict_review:
            PullRequestCodeCommented(pull_request: pr, comment: remark)
}

-- Delete a review (pending draft or submitted): the reviewer or an instance admin.
-- Deleting an official review restores `is_official` on the reviewer's latest
-- remaining approve/request_changes review.
-- from: models/issues/review.go:820
rule UserDeletesReview {
    when: UserDeletesReview(user, pr, doomed)
    requires: doomed.pull_request = pr
    requires: user = doomed.reviewer or user.is_admin
    ensures:
        for thread in CodeConversations where review = doomed:
            not exists thread
        for remark in ReviewComments where review = doomed:
            not exists remark
        not exists doomed
        if doomed.is_official:
            ReviewerOfficialStandingRecalculated(pull_request: doomed.pull_request, reviewer: doomed.reviewer)
    @guidance
        -- API: DELETE /repos/{o}/{r}/pulls/{index}/reviews/{id}. Pending reviews
        -- are visible (and deletable) only by their author and instance admins.
}

-- from: models/issues/review.go:650
rule RestoreLatestOfficialReview {
    when: ReviewerOfficialStandingRecalculated(pull_request, reviewer)
    let pr = pull_request
    let latest = latest_blocking_review_of(pr, reviewer)
    requires: exists latest
    requires: pr.is_official_reviewer(reviewer)
    ensures: latest.is_official = true
}

-- Repository admins dismiss an approve/request_changes review (and the
-- reviewer's earlier ones) with a message, while the PR is open and unmerged.
-- from: services/pull/review.go:499
rule RepoAdminDismissesReview {
    when: RepoAdminDismissesReview(admin, pr, review, message)
    requires: review.pull_request = pr
    requires: is_repo_admin(admin, pr.base_repository)
    requires: review.is_blocking_verdict
    requires: pr.is_open
    requires: not pr.is_merged
    requires: review.is_dismissed = false
    ensures:
        review.is_dismissed = true
        for earlier in Reviews where pull_request = pr and status = submitted and reviewer = review.reviewer:
            earlier.is_dismissed = true
        issues/Comment.created(issue: pr.issue, poster: admin, kind: dismiss_review, content: message, review: review,
            content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        ReviewDismissed(review: review, dismisser: admin, message: message)
    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /{o}/{r}/pulls/dismiss_review; API: POST
        -- pulls/{index}/reviews/{id}/dismissals. A dismissal re-evaluates auto-merge.
}

-- from: routers/api/v1/repo/pull_review.go:1024
rule RepoAdminUndismissesReview {
    when: RepoAdminUndismissesReview(admin, pr, review)
    requires: review.pull_request = pr
    requires: is_repo_admin(admin, pr.base_repository)
    requires: review.is_blocking_verdict
    requires: pr.is_open
    requires: not pr.is_merged
    requires: review.is_dismissed = true
    ensures: review.is_dismissed = false
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: review requests
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Request a review from a user. Requesting again from someone who already
-- reviewed is a re-request (only while the PR is open and unmerged); a request
-- that is already pending is a no-op.
-- from: services/issue/assignee.go:84
rule UserRequestsReview {
    when: UserRequestsReview(user, pr, requested)
    requires: pr.base_repository.is_archived = false
    requires: is_organization(requested) = false
    requires: can_read_pulls(requested, pr.base_repository)
    requires: requested != pr.issue.poster
    requires: pr.may_change_review_requests(user)
    requires: not exists ReviewRequest{pull_request: pr, reviewer: requested}
    requires: (pr.is_open and not pr.is_merged) or not has_submitted_review(pr, requested)
    let official = pr.is_official_reviewer(requested)
    ensures:
        if official:
            for earlier in Reviews where pull_request = pr and status = submitted and reviewer = requested:
                earlier.is_official = false
        ReviewRequest.created(pull_request: pr, reviewer: requested, team: null, requested_by: user,
            is_official: official, created_at: now)
        issues/Comment.created(issue: pr.issue, poster: user, kind: review_request, content: requested.name,
            content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        if user != requested:
            ReviewRequested(pull_request: pr, requester: user, reviewer: requested)
    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /{o}/{r}/issues/request_review (reviewer id, action attach);
        -- API: POST pulls/{index}/requested_reviewers {reviewers, team_reviewers}.
        -- With a token, the token's access must reach write.
}

-- Withdraw a user review request: anyone who may change requests, or the
-- requested reviewer themselves.
-- from: models/issues/review.go:612
rule UserWithdrawsReviewRequest {
    when: UserWithdrawsReviewRequest(user, pr, request)
    requires: request.pull_request = pr
    requires: request.reviewer != null
    requires: pr.may_change_review_requests(user) or user = request.reviewer
    ensures:
        not exists request
        issues/Comment.created(issue: pr.issue, poster: user, kind: review_request, content: request.reviewer.name,
            content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        ReviewerOfficialStandingRecalculated(pull_request: pr, reviewer: request.reviewer)
        ReviewRequestRemoved(pull_request: pr, doer: user, reviewer: request.reviewer)
}

-- Request a review from a team of the organization owning the repository. For
-- a private repository the team must have access to it.
-- from: services/issue/assignee.go:160
rule UserRequestsTeamReview {
    when: UserRequestsTeamReview(user, pr, team)
    requires: pr.base_repository.is_archived = false
    requires: pr.base_repository.owner_org = team.organization
    requires: not pr.base_repository.is_private or team_has_repository(team, pr.base_repository)
    requires: pr.may_change_review_requests(user)
    requires: not exists ReviewRequest{pull_request: pr, team: team}
    ensures: ReviewRequest.created(pull_request: pr, reviewer: null, team: team, requested_by: user,
        is_official: team_is_official_reviewer(team, pr), created_at: now)
    ensures: issues/Comment.created(issue: pr.issue, poster: user, kind: review_request, content: team.name,
        content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
    ensures: TeamReviewRequested(pull_request: pr, requester: user, team: team)
    @guidance
        -- Team members (except the poster) are told individually. A team is an
        -- official reviewer when the rule's approvals allowlist contains it, or
        -- (allowlist disabled) when it has write access to code; without a
        -- protection rule team requests are never official.
}

-- from: models/issues/review.go:705
rule UserWithdrawsTeamReviewRequest {
    when: UserWithdrawsTeamReviewRequest(user, pr, request)
    requires: request.pull_request = pr
    requires: request.team != null
    requires: pr.may_change_review_requests(user)
    ensures: not exists request
    ensures: issues/Comment.created(issue: pr.issue, poster: user, kind: review_request, content: request.team.name,
        content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
    ensures: TeamReviewRequestRemoved(pull_request: pr, doer: user, team: request.team)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: conversations, suggestions, viewed files
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: models/issues/review.go:751
rule UserResolvesCodeConversation {
    when: UserResolvesCodeConversation(user, pr, thread)
    requires: thread.pull_request = pr
    requires: pr.base_repository.is_archived = false
    requires: pr.may_resolve_conversations(user)
    requires: thread.resolved_by = null
    ensures: thread.resolved_by = user
    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /{o}/{r}/issues/resolve_conversation (action=Resolve|UnResolve).
}

-- from: models/issues/review.go:751
rule UserUnresolvesCodeConversation {
    when: UserUnresolvesCodeConversation(user, pr, thread)
    requires: thread.pull_request = pr
    requires: pr.base_repository.is_archived = false
    requires: pr.may_resolve_conversations(user)
    requires: thread.resolved_by != null
    ensures: thread.resolved_by = null
}

-- Apply one or more ```suggestion blocks as a single commit on the head branch.
-- Each suggestion must belong to this PR, be published (not pending), be on
-- the proposed side, and its anchored lines must be unchanged at the current
-- head; suggestions may not overlap; binary, LFS and over-size files refuse.
-- Authors of the applied suggestions become Co-authored-by trailers.
-- Conversations the applier may resolve are resolved.
-- from: services/repository/files/suggestion.go:65
rule UserAppliesSuggestions {
    when: UserAppliesSuggestions(user, pr, threads, summary, message)
    requires: threads.count >= 1 and threads.count <= config.max_suggestions_per_apply
    requires: threads.all(t => t.pull_request = pr)
    requires: threads.all(t => t.review.status = submitted and t.side = proposed and t.line > 0)
    requires: threads.all(t => suggestion_applicable(t, pr.head_commit_sha))
    requires: not suggestions_overlap(threads)
    requires: pr.head_is_editable_by(user)
    requires: within_quota(pr.head_repository)
    ensures:
        for thread in threads:
            if pr.may_resolve_conversations(user):
                thread.resolved_by = user
        PullRequestHeadMoved(pull_request: pr, pusher: user, old_commit_sha: pr.head_commit_sha,
            new_commit_sha: suggestion_commit(pr, threads, summary, message))
        SuggestionsApplied(pull_request: pr, doer: user, conversations: threads)
    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /pulls/{index}/files/reviews/apply_suggestion
        -- {comment_ids (<= 100, deduplicated), commit_summary, commit_message}.
        -- The commit goes through the web-editor path of the head repository
        -- (protected-branch, signing and quota checks of code apply).
}

-- Mark files of the current head as viewed / not viewed for oneself.
-- from: routers/web/repo/pull_review.go:458
rule UserMarksFilesViewed {
    when: UserMarksFilesViewed(user, pr, paths, viewed)
    requires: can_read_pulls(user, pr.base_repository)
    ensures:
        for path in paths:
            FileViewState.created(pull_request: pr, user: user, commit_sha: pr.head_commit_sha, path: path,
                state: if viewed: viewed else: unviewed, updated_at: now)
    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /{o}/{r}/pulls/{index}/viewed-files {files: {path: bool},
        -- headCommitSHA}. One record per (user, PR, head commit), merged with
        -- the newest earlier record: files viewed at an older head whose diff
        -- changed since are shown as has_changed. has_changed cannot be set by
        -- users.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- At most one open, unmerged pull request per (head repository, head branch,
-- base repository, base branch, flow).
-- from: models/issues/pull.go:509
invariant OneOpenPullRequestPerHeadAndBase {
    for a in PullRequests:
        for b in PullRequests:
            (a != b and a.issue.status = open and b.issue.status = open
                and a.status != merged and a.status != manually_merged
                and b.status != merged and b.status != manually_merged
                and a.head_repository = b.head_repository and a.head_branch = b.head_branch
                and a.base_repository = b.base_repository and a.base_branch = b.base_branch
                and a.flow = b.flow) implies false
}

-- Every pull request's conversation is a pull-request issue of its base repository.
-- from: models/issues/pull.go:460
invariant PullRequestConversationIsAPullIssue {
    for pr in PullRequests:
        pr.issue.is_pull = true and pr.issue.repository = pr.base_repository
}

-- A merged pull request's conversation is closed.
-- from: models/issues/pull.go:399
invariant MergedPullRequestsAreClosed {
    for pr in PullRequests:
        (pr.status = merged or pr.status = manually_merged) implies pr.issue.status = closed
}

-- At most one scheduled auto-merge per pull request.
-- from: models/pull/automerge.go:47
invariant OneAutoMergePerPullRequest {
    for a in AutoMerges:
        for b in AutoMerges:
            (a != b) implies a.pull_request != b.pull_request
}

-- At most one pending review per reviewer per pull request.
-- from: models/issues/review.go:316
invariant OnePendingReviewPerReviewer {
    for a in Reviews:
        for b in Reviews:
            (a != b and a.status = pending and b.status = pending and a.pull_request = b.pull_request) implies a.reviewer != b.reviewer
}

-- A poster never approves or requests changes on their own pull request.
-- from: routers/web/repo/pull_review.go:400
invariant NoSelfApproval {
    for review in Reviews:
        (review.status = submitted and (review.kind = approve or review.kind = request_changes))
            implies review.reviewer != review.pull_request.issue.poster
}

-- At most one official approve/request_changes review per reviewer per PR.
-- from: models/issues/review.go:366
invariant OneOfficialReviewPerReviewer {
    for a in Reviews:
        for b in Reviews:
            (a != b and a.is_official and b.is_official and a.pull_request = b.pull_request) implies a.reviewer != b.reviewer
}

-- A review request names exactly one of a user or a team.
-- from: models/issues/review.go:286
invariant ReviewRequestNamesOneParty {
    for request in ReviewRequests:
        (request.reviewer = null) != (request.team = null)
}

-- A code comment's line range never exceeds the configured maximum.
-- from: services/pull/review.go:109
invariant CodeCommentRangeWithinLimit {
    for thread in CodeConversations:
        thread.extra_lines >= 0
}

-- A conversation's comments belong to the conversation's review.
-- from: models/issues/comment_code.go:214
invariant ConversationCommentsShareTheReview {
    for remark in ReviewComments:
        remark.review = remark.conversation.review
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Anyone who can read the pull-request unit of a repository (including the
-- anonymous visitor of a public repository, per access).
actor PullRequestReader {
    within: PullRequest
    identified_by: accounts/User where can_read_pulls(this, within.base_repository)
}

-- A signed-in user looking at a repository they may propose changes to.
actor Contributor {
    within: repositories/Repository
    identified_by: accounts/User where can_read_pulls(this, within) and can_read_code(this, within)
}

-- The poster of a pull request.
actor PullRequestAuthor {
    within: PullRequest
    identified_by: accounts/User where this = within.issue.poster
}

-- Someone who may merge the pull request (code writer or merge allowlist).
actor PullRequestMaintainer {
    within: PullRequest
    identified_by: accounts/User where within.may_merge(this) or can_write_pulls(this, within.base_repository)
}

-- An admin of the base repository (dismisses reviews, merges anyway).
actor PullRequestRepoAdmin {
    within: PullRequest
    identified_by: accounts/User where is_repo_admin(this, within.base_repository)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Opening a pull request: the compare page and the create endpoint.
surface PullRequestComposer {
    facing contributor: Contributor
    context repository: repositories/Repository

    exposes:
        repository.default_branch
        repository.is_archived

    provides:
        UserOpensPullRequest(contributor, repository, base_branch, head_repository, head_branch, title, body, allow_maintainer_edit)
            when repository.is_archived = false

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET/POST /{o}/{r}/compare/{base}...{head} (also
        -- {headOwner}:{head}, {headOwner}/{headRepo}:{head}), offering the
        -- base repository's root repository and the user's own fork as head
        -- candidates, the commits and diff, an existing open PR for the same
        -- pair, the PR template, and "allow edits from maintainers" defaulted
        -- from settings. API: POST /repos/{o}/{r}/pulls,
        -- GET /repos/{o}/{r}/pulls/{base}/{head} (find PR by base and head).
}

-- What anyone who can read the pull requests of the base repository sees and
-- may do on a pull request.
surface PullRequestPage {
    facing viewer: PullRequestReader
    context pr: PullRequest

    exposes:
        pr.issue.title
        pr.issue.status
        pr.flow
        pr.head_repository.name
        pr.head_branch
        pr.base_branch
        pr.head_commit_sha
        pr.merge_base_sha
        pr.status
        pr.conflicted_files
        pr.changed_protected_files
        pr.commits_ahead
        pr.commits_behind
        pr.allow_maintainer_edit
        pr.is_work_in_progress
        pr.head_branch_present
        pr.required_checks_pass
        pr.approval_count
        pr.protection_satisfied
        pr.merged_commit_sha when pr.is_merged
        pr.merger when pr.is_merged
        pr.merged_at when pr.is_merged
        pr.auto_merge.scheduled_by
        for review in pr.submitted_reviews:
            review.reviewer
            review.kind
            review.body
            review.is_official
            review.is_stale
            review.is_dismissed
        for request in pr.review_requests:
            request.reviewer
            request.team
        for thread in pr.conversations:
            thread.path
            thread.line
            thread.side
            thread.is_outdated
            thread.resolved_by
        for remark in pr.conversations.comments:
            remark.body
            remark.poster

    provides:
        UserSubmitsReview(viewer, pr, verdict, body, commit_sha)
        UserAddsPendingCodeComment(viewer, pr, path, line, side, extra_lines, body)
        UserPostsSingleCodeComment(viewer, pr, path, line, side, extra_lines, body)
        UserRepliesToCodeConversation(viewer, pr, thread, body)
        UserMarksFilesViewed(viewer, pr, paths, viewed)
        UserRequestsReview(viewer, pr, reviewer) when pr.may_change_review_requests(viewer)
        UserRequestsTeamReview(viewer, pr, team) when pr.may_change_review_requests(viewer)
        UserWithdrawsReviewRequest(viewer, pr, request)
        UserWithdrawsTeamReviewRequest(viewer, pr, request) when pr.may_change_review_requests(viewer)
        UserResolvesCodeConversation(viewer, pr, thread) when pr.may_resolve_conversations(viewer)
        UserUnresolvesCodeConversation(viewer, pr, thread) when pr.may_resolve_conversations(viewer)
        UserEditsReviewComment(viewer, pr, comment, body)
        UserDeletesReviewComment(viewer, pr, comment)
        UserDeletesReview(viewer, pr, review)
        UserAppliesSuggestions(viewer, pr, threads, summary, message) when pr.head_is_editable_by(viewer)
        UserUpdatesPullRequestBranch(viewer, pr, style) when pr.is_open and pr.commits_behind > 0
        UserChangesPullRequestTarget(viewer, pr, new_base_branch) when pr.may_manage(viewer)
        UserClosesPullRequest(viewer, pr) when pr.may_manage(viewer) and pr.is_open
        UserReopensPullRequest(viewer, pr) when pr.may_manage(viewer) and not pr.is_open
        UserDeletesPullRequestHeadBranch(viewer, pr) when pr.is_merged or not pr.is_open

    @guarantee PendingReviewsArePrivate
        -- A pending review, its conversations and comments are visible only to
        -- its author (and instance admins through the API); they appear to
        -- others only once submitted.

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /{o}/{r}/pulls/{index} (conversation), /commits,
        -- /commits/{sha}, /files, /files/{sha}, /files/{from}..{to} (diffs,
        -- optionally hiding outdated comments), /pulls/{index}.diff and
        -- .patch (download; ?binary=true), /pulls/{index}.rss|.atom.
        -- API: GET pulls, pulls/{index}, pulls/{index}.diff|.patch,
        -- pulls/{index}/commits, pulls/{index}/files, pulls/{index}/reviews,
        -- reviews/{id}, reviews/{id}/comments, pulls/{index}/merge (is merged),
        -- pulls/pinned. Reading requires the pull-request unit to be enabled,
        -- the repository not a mirror and not empty, and read access to code
        -- for the API.
}

-- A reviewer's own draft review.
surface DraftReviewPanel {
    facing author: accounts/User
    context draft: Review where status = pending and reviewer = author

    exposes:
        draft.body
        draft.commit_sha
        for remark in draft.comments:
            remark.body
            remark.conversation.path
            remark.conversation.line

    provides:
        UserSubmitsDraftReview(author, draft, verdict, body, commit_sha)
        UserDeletesReview(author, draft.pull_request, draft)

    @guarantee OnlyTheAuthorSeesADraft
        -- A pending review exists for nobody but its author (instance admins
        -- may list and delete it through the API).
}

-- What maintainers (people who may merge) can do.
surface PullRequestMergeBox {
    facing maintainer: PullRequestMaintainer
    context pr: PullRequest

    exposes:
        pr.status
        pr.is_work_in_progress
        pr.protection_satisfied
        pr.has_enough_approvals
        pr.required_checks_pass
        pr.blocked_by_rejection
        pr.blocked_by_official_requests
        pr.blocked_by_outdated_branch
        pr.blocked_by_protected_files
        pr.changed_protected_files
        pr.conflicted_files
        pr.auto_merge.style
        pr.auto_merge.scheduled_by

    provides:
        UserMergesPullRequest(maintainer, pr, style, title, message, expected_head_sha, delete_branch_after_merge, force_merge)
            when pr.is_open and not pr.is_merged
        UserSchedulesAutoMerge(maintainer, pr, style, message, delete_branch_after_merge)
            when pr.is_open and not exists pr.auto_merge
        UserCancelsAutoMerge(maintainer, pr) when exists pr.auto_merge
        UserMarksPullRequestManuallyMerged(maintainer, pr, commit_sha) when pr.is_open and not pr.is_merged
        UserChangesPullRequestTarget(maintainer, pr, new_base_branch) when pr.is_open
        UserUpdatesPullRequestBranch(maintainer, pr, style) when pr.commits_behind > 0
        UserDeletesPullRequestHeadBranch(maintainer, pr) when pr.is_merged

    timeout:
        AutoMergeExecutes

    @guidance
        -- The merge box lists each unmet gate (WIP, conflicts, checking,
        -- status checks with required-context glob matching, approvals,
        -- requested changes, official review requests, outdated branch,
        -- protected files, open dependencies) and offers "merge anyway" to
        -- those who may bypass protection. The default style is
        -- settings.default_merge_style, else config.default_merge_style; the
        -- default message comes from MergeMessageTemplate.
}

-- What only the poster controls.
surface PullRequestAuthorControls {
    facing author: PullRequestAuthor
    context pr: PullRequest

    exposes:
        pr.allow_maintainer_edit
        pr.is_from_fork

    provides:
        AuthorSetsMaintainerEdits(author, pr, allow)
        UserChangesPullRequestTarget(author, pr, new_base_branch) when pr.is_open
        UserClosesPullRequest(author, pr) when pr.is_open
        UserReopensPullRequest(author, pr) when not pr.is_open and not pr.is_merged
        UserRequestsReview(author, pr, reviewer)
        UserCancelsAutoMerge(author, pr) when exists pr.auto_merge and pr.auto_merge.scheduled_by = author
}

-- Repository administrators moderating reviews.
surface ReviewModeration {
    facing admin: PullRequestRepoAdmin
    context pr: PullRequest

    exposes:
        for review in pr.submitted_reviews:
            review.reviewer
            review.kind
            review.is_dismissed

    provides:
        RepoAdminDismissesReview(admin, pr, review, message) when pr.is_open and not pr.is_merged
        RepoAdminUndismissesReview(admin, pr, review) when pr.is_open and not pr.is_merged
        UserMergesPullRequest(admin, pr, style, title, message, expected_head_sha, delete_branch_after_merge, force_merge)
            when pr.may_bypass_protection(admin)
}

-- Instance administrators.
surface SiteAdminReviewControls {
    facing admin: access/SiteAdmin
    context review: Review

    exposes:
        review.reviewer
        review.status

    provides:
        UserDeletesReview(admin, review.pull_request, review)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------

deferred MergeabilityCheck.outcome      -- see: three-way merge / merge-tree semantics in services/pull/patch.go
deferred MergeExecution.commit          -- see: services/pull/merge_*.go per style

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "Scheduling auto-merge when one already exists: the web form silently replaces it, the API refuses with a conflict. Which should the rebuild do?"
open question "Closing a pull request leaves its scheduled auto-merge in place (it can fire again after reopening). Should closing cancel the schedule?"
open question "A failing auto-merge is only logged; should the scheduler be told and the schedule removed?"
open question "Is the 'ancestor' status (head already contained in base, autodetect off) worth keeping distinct from 'empty'?"
open question "Submitting reviews and code comments is allowed on closed and merged pull requests; intended?"
open question "Review requests may be added by any collaborator or org team member with pull-request read access, even without write access; intended?"
open question "Code-comment outdating is skipped for AGit pushes in Forgejo (TODO in the code); the spec applies it to every head move."
open question "Update-branch is unsupported for AGit pull requests; should a rebuild support it?"
open question "Squash-merge author: the PR poster's commit identity is preferred over their primary email; keep this heuristic?"
open question "Mergeability is checked synchronously at creation and asynchronously afterwards; the spec makes every check asynchronous."
open question "Should merge-message templates live only in the repository (.forgejo/default_merge_message) or also at instance level?"

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Requests to other modules
------------------------------------------------------------

-- REQUEST code/ProtectedBranch: pulls reads repository, status_check_enabled, status_check_contexts (globs over CommitStatus.context, evaluated by required_status_checks_pass), required_approvals, block_on_rejected_reviews, block_on_official_review_requests, block_on_outdated_branch, dismiss_stale_approvals, ignore_stale_approvals, apply_to_admins, protected_file_patterns, allows_merge_by(user), counts_approval_of(user) — all present; also needs protection_for(repository, branch) as the shared "first matching rule" function and rule_matches_branch(rule, branch).
-- REQUEST code: AgitPullRequestRequested should only fire when the pusher can read pull requests (pulls re-checks); AgitPullRequestHeadPushed for refs/pull/<n>/head must require code write or the PR poster (pulls re-checks).
-- REQUEST code: react to HeadBranchDeletionRequested(user, branch) by deleting the branch as UserDeletesBranch does (done: code/PullRequestHeadBranchIsDeleted).
-- REQUEST code: the merge push (Push.merging_pull) pre-receive should apply pulls/PullRequest.may_merge and protection_satisfied minus protected files.
-- REQUEST issues: UserClosesIssue / UserReopensIssue should not apply to pull-request conversations (is_pull) — pulls owns UserClosesPullRequest / UserReopensPullRequest with PR-specific guards (merged, duplicate head/base, deleted branches) — or should defer to them.
-- REQUEST issues: Comment needs `review` for kinds review/dismiss_review/code and `old_ref`/`new_ref` for change_target_branch/delete_branch (present); review_request comments for removals carry the reviewer/team name.
-- REQUEST issues: next_issue_index(repository) for PR conversations; ConversationClosedByMerge on PullRequestMerged(pull_request, merger) closes the conversation, stops the merger's stopwatch and applies closing/reopening keywords (as written).
-- REQUEST issues/IssueTitleChanged(issue, doer, old_title): WIP prefix removal => ready for review (present).
-- REQUEST repositories/RepoUnit.pull_request_settings (PullRequestSettings value: allow_* styles, autodetect_manual_merge, allow_rebase_update, ignore_whitespace_conflicts, default_*): read through merge_style_allowed(repository, style) and autodetects_manual_merge(repository).
-- REQUEST repositories/RepositoryDeleted(repository, doer): pulls closes outgoing PRs before purge.
-- REQUEST accounts/UserRenamed(user, old_name, new_name): AGit head branch prefixes.
-- REQUEST accounts/UserBlock: is_blocked_by_owner(repository, user) as used by issues.
-- REQUEST keys: merge_signing_satisfied(pr, user, style) — when the protection rule requires signed commits, a merge that creates a commit (every style but fast_forward_only) must be signable under [repository.signing] MERGES.
-- REQUEST quota: within_quota(repository) for merges, branch updates and applied suggestions (size:git:all of the target repository owner).
-- REQUEST all consumers: the journey walker binds chained-trigger parameters BY NAME, so rules reacting to pulls triggers should use the emitted parameter names (e.g. `when: pulls/PullRequestMerged(pull_request, merger)`, not `(pr, merger)`).
-- REQUEST notifications / webhooks / actions: consume the Emits list (names and parameters reconciled here: PullRequestOpened(pull_request), PullRequestMerged(pull_request, merger), ReviewSubmitted(review), ReviewRequested(pull_request, requester, reviewer), ReviewRequestRemoved(pull_request, doer, reviewer), PullRequestSynchronized(pull_request, doer)).
